ipd: opt-in scatter-gather / software GSO on the front-panel netdevs

The netdevs advertise no features, so TCP hands the driver one linear
MTU-sized skb per segment and every segment walks TCP output, the bond,
the qdisc and the driver on its own (TX-3: 3 descriptors per packet,
~1417 bytes per packet over 134M packets).

inno_enet_tx() already emits one descriptor per skb fragment.  Offer
NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_HW_CSUM in hw_features (NOT enabled by default) and
resolve CHECKSUM_PARTIAL in software with skb_checksum_help().  With
"ethtool -K <dev> tx on sg on" the stack builds 64k GSO skbs and segments
them just before the driver.

Default off because the multi-fragment descriptor path of the ASIC's DMA
engine has not been exercised on this hardware; with the features off the
only added code on the TX path is one ip_summed test.

Not verified on hardware when written.

--- a/inno_enet.c
+++ b/inno_enet.c
@@ -267,6 +267,15 @@
         return NETDEV_TX_OK;
     }
 
+    /* The ASIC does not checksum for us.  NETIF_F_HW_CSUM is only offered
+     * so that the stack will do scatter-gather / software GSO (see
+     * inno_netdev_create()); fill the checksum in here. */
+    if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL && skb_checksum_help(skb)) {
+        idev->inno_stats.tx_ring_stats[tx_ring->num].drops++;
+        dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+        return NETDEV_TX_OK;
+    }
+
     /* The completion NAPI is behind (ring more than 3/4 used): reap
      * finished descriptors from here rather than run into a full ring.
      * trylock: if the NAPI is already reaping there is nothing to add. */
@@ -2356,6 +2365,16 @@
     enet->idev = idev;
     enet->sysport = ioctl->sysport;
 
+    /* Opt-in (default off): "ethtool -K <dev> tx on sg on".  The TX path
+     * already maps one descriptor per skb fragment, and the checksum is
+     * computed in software in inno_enet_tx(), so with these on TCP hands
+     * down 64k GSO skbs that are segmented right before the driver: one
+     * stack/bond/qdisc traversal per ~44 MTU frames instead of one each. */
+    idev->sysport_devs[ioctl->sysport]->hw_features |=
+        NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;
+    idev->sysport_devs[ioctl->sysport]->vlan_features |=
+        NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;
+
     idev->sysport_devs[ioctl->sysport]->watchdog_timeo = (HZ >> 1);
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 10, 0)
     idev->sysport_devs[ioctl->sysport]->min_mtu = ETH_MIN_MTU;
